# decision Bundler git dependencies are explicit Gemfile entries

The Gem adapter owns one top-level `gem` declaration in `Gemfile`. Locked wiring uses the full
commit as `ref`; floating wiring uses the declared ref as `branch`. An export subdirectory adds
Bundler's native `glob: "<path>/*.gemspec"`. The adapter leaves `Gemfile.lock` downstream so it
does not resolve or rewrite unrelated gems.

# test Gem adapter

- Fixture/golden wiring is idempotent and preserves unrelated Ruby text and comments.
- Drift checks both the normalized Git URL and locked revision.
- Unwire removes only the named gem declaration.

# decision Refresh prerequisite

`Refresh` checks `bundle` through the shared prerequisite contract before doing any work.
